  "sources": [
    {
      "title": "India's GDP to grow 7.1-7.3% in FY27, pvt investment to revive: Deloitte",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/economy/news/india-s-gdp-to-grow-7-1-7-3-in-fy27-pvt-investment-to-revive-deloitte-126101601184_1.html",
      "description": "Deloitte India has raised its FY27 growth forecast from 6.5-6.8 per cent, citing sustained private demand and improving investment conditions, while flagging geopolitical risks.",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-10-16T13:43:23"
    },
    {
      "title": "India GDP to grow 7.1-7.3% in FY27 on private investment revival: Deloitte",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/economy/news/india-gdp-to-grow-7-1-7-3-in-fy27-on-private-investment-revival-deloitte-126101600332_1.html",
      "description": "The Indian economy is expected to grow by 7.1-7.3 per cent in the current fiscal, with a sustained revival in private investment providing an additional source of demand, Deloitte India said on Friday.\nHowever, geopolitical tensions, volatile energy prices and trade disruptions pose risks to the growth outlook, it added.\nDeloitte India Economist Rumki Majumdar said over the past decade, India's growth has rested on resilient household spending and sustained investment push in public infrastructure. Businesses now have better connectivity, healthier balance sheets, and higher capacity utilisation, which strengthens the case for expansion.\n\"The question is whether these conditions will encourage private investment to play a larger role in boosting growth in the coming years. Recent indicators offer grounds for optimism. Gross fixed capital formation grew by 11.9 per cent in the first quarter of FY 2026-27, its fastest expansion in four years,\" Majumdar said.\nDeloitte Economic Outlook",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-10-16T05:41:22"
    }
  ]
